spans.s:
पुरा॑ adv. formerly, once upon a time, of yore;
 up to the
present time, hitherto (w. pres. ±स्म);
 at first, firstly;
 soon,
shortly (w. pres.);
 w. a neg. never. — As a conj. ere, before (w. pres.
±न, मा, or यदि);
 as a prep. before, from, except, without (abl.).

पूर a. filling, completing, satisfying (—˚);
 m. completion,
fulfilment, satisfaction;
 flood, gush, stream;
 a cake.

पु॑रंधि a. prolific (lit. bearing a body), bounteous,
liberal;
 f. liberality, also = seq.

पुरश्च॑रण a. making preparations for (—˚), abstr.
˚ता f.;
 n. a preparatory rite.

पुरस्कृत a. placed before, appointed, chosen,
preferred, honoured;
 accompanied by, possessed of, connected or occupied
with;
 n. adv. in company with (—˚).

पुराण॑ f. ई former, ancient, old;
 n. things of the past,
ancient history or legend, T. of a class of sacred works.

पुरातन f. ई existing from of old, former, ancient,
loc. in the times of old;
 m. pl. the ancients.

पुरावृत्त a. happened long since, past, ancient;
 n. past
event, old story.

पु॑रीष n. crumbling or loose earth, rubbish, excrement,
ordure;
 poss. ˚वन्त्.

पुरु॑ f. पूर्वी॑ much, many (in l. l. only ˚—);
 m. N. of an
ancient king;
 n. पुरु॑ or पुरू॑ much, often, greatly;
 superl.
पुरुत॑म or पुरुत॑म very much or many, very frequent, often
repeated, n. adv.

पूरु॑ m. man, people (coll.);
 N. of a tribe & an ancient
prince.

पु॑रुष (पू॑रुष) m. man, human being, male, person,
individual of a cert. generation;
 man = hero;
 man = servant, attendant;
official, agent;
 the primal man or spirit;
 the life-giving principle in
man and other beings;
 the supreme spirit or soul of the universe. —f.
पुरुषी॑ a woman.

पुरुषकार m. manly deed, human effort;
 manhood,
virility.

पुरुषार्थ m. any object or aim of men;
 ˚प्रयोजन n.
means for obtaining it.

पुरुषोत्तम m. the best of men or of servants;
 the
supreme spirit (Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa).

पुरूर॑वस् a. crying loudly;
 m. N. of a myth. king and
hero.

पुरोगव॑ m. forerunner (lit. fore-bull);
 leader (f.
ई).

पुरोडा॑श् (पुरो˚ळा॑श्;
 nom. ˚ळा॑स्) m. sacrificial cake,
oblation i.g.

पुरोभाग m. forepart;
 obtrusiveness, impudence,
malevolence, envy.

पुरोरथ॑ a. whose chariot is foremost;
 i.g. excelling,
superior.

पुरोरु॑च् a. shining in front or before;
 f. N. of cert.
sacred formulas.

पुरो॑हित a. set before, commissioned, appointed;
 m. an
appointed priest, esp. house-priest of a prince.

पूरक a. = prec. (—˚ or *gen.);
 m. stream, gush, f.
पूरिका a sort of cake.

पूरयितृ (पूरयि˚तृक*) a. filling up;
 m. fulfiller,
satisfier.

पूर्ण॑ a. filled, full;
 full of, rich in (instr., gen., or
—˚), complete, abundant;
 fulfilled, accomplished, satisfied.

पूर्णकुम्भ m. a full cup or jar;
 m. n. a breach or
gap of a cert. shape.

पूर्ण॑मास m. the same, full-moon sacrifice;
 f. ई the
day or night of full moon.

पूर्त॑ a. filled, full of (gen.);
 bestowed, fulfilled;
 n. =
seq.

पू॑र्व a. being before (sp. & t.), fore, first, eastern, to
the east of (abl.);
 prior, preceding, ancient, previous to, earlier than
(abl. or —˚, often ˚— or —˚ w. pp. in the sense of an adv., e.g.
पूर्वोक्त or उक्तपूर्व spoken before or already);
 accompanied by,
following;
 with, under, according to (—˚);
 w. वयस् n. youth;
 w.
आयुस् n. old age. —m. elder brother, pl. the ancestors or ancients. f.
पूर्वा (±दिश्) the east. n. forepart, as adv. in front, before (as
prep. w. abl.), first, previously, already, long since;
 —˚ accompanied
by etc. (cf. adj. —˚). पूर्व उत्तर former-latter, n. adv.
first-last;
 अद्य पूर्वम् until now, hitherto.

पूर्वक f. पूर्विका earlier^1, former, previous;
 —˚ adj. &
n. adv. accompanied by etc. = prec.;
 m. ancestor, forefather.
[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.

पूर्वज॑ a. born or produced before, former, previous,
ancient, very old, the elder or
[]
eldest;
 m. forefather, ancestor;
eldest (elder) brother.

पूर्वपक्ष॑ m. the fore part or side;
 the first half of
a month or year;
 action or law-suit;
 the first objection (ph.).

पूर्वपुरुष m. forefather, ancestor;
 the primeval
spirit i.e. Brahman.

पूर्वपूर्व a. each previous or former one;
 m. pl. the
forefathers.

1 पूर्वरूप॑ n. indication, forerunner, prognostic of
(प्रति);
 a cert. figure of speech.

पूर्वार्ध॑ m. (n.) the front or upper part;
 the east
side;
 the first half.

पूर्वाह्ण॑ m. forenoon (lit. earlier day);
 loc. early in
the morning.

पू॑र्वेण adv. in front;
 before, to the east of (acc. or
gen.).

पूर्व्य॑ (पू॑र्व्य) a. previous, former, ancient, old;
first, best, next, nearest;
 n. adv. formerly, long, since, hitherto.
